# Typed impact numbers (server/README.md "Typed impact numbers", client base patch 0100). Every damage, heal, mana and
# experience text message (0xB4, modes 23..29) carries three more fields after its value / colour pairs and before the
# text: u16 percent (the value as a share of the target's maximum health, mana for mana, the level's experience for an
# experience gain; x100, rounded up), u8 type (ChaosImpactType: 0 normal, 1 critical, 2 condition tick, 3 mana drain,
# 4 mana gain, 5 energy shield, 6+ free for scripts) and u32 creature id (the creature the number belongs to; the
# client draws it on that creature). One set per message: both pairs of a hit share it. Only a client that asks for it
# gets the new layout: our client sets bit 7 (CHAOS_CAPABILITY_IMPACT_TEXT) of the capability byte it sends after its
# markers in the login packet, and sendFeatures then announces GameChaosImpactText (155); every other client keeps the
# old layout, so an older client works with this engine and this client works with an older engine.
# CombatDamage::critical (combat.cpp) gives type 1; CombatDamage::firstOrigin keeps ORIGIN_CONDITION across the
# onHealthChange / onManaChange re-entry (which sets origin to ORIGIN_NONE), so a tick keeps type 2 after a script ran.
# Lua: player:sendTextMessage(type, text, pos, value, color, secondaryValue, secondaryColor, percent, typeId, creature)
# (a creature given but gone: false). Apply in the server source root after 0001-0050: patch -p1 < 0051-typed-impact-numbers.patch, then
# rebuild everything (TextMessage, CombatDamage and ProtocolGame change layout).
